  "summary": "The use of rapid, high-intensity light flashes to create the illusion of frozen motion in performance environments.",
  "description": "Strobe freeze employs precisely timed strobe lights that flash at frequencies matching or harmonizing with movement, creating the visual effect of time suspension or mechanical motion. This technique originated in experimental theater and rock concerts of the 1960s and became particularly associated with punk and industrial subcultures seeking dramatic visual impact.",
